<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<section xml:id="curry" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Curry - Red Dwarf Chicken</title>

  <p>
    Ingredients:
  </p>
  <tabular>
    <row>
      <cell><m>1 \frac{1}{2}</m> cups rice</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon turmeric (optional)</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>1 \frac{1}{2}</m> pounds chicken, cut into thin strips or cubed</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
    <cell>1 onion, finely sliced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 to 3 cloves garlic, minced</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 tablespoon canola oil</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 teaspoon curry paste</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>4 ounces chicken broth (1 tablespoon "Better than Boullion")</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>1 can coconut milk</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell><m>\frac{1}{2}</m> to 1 teaspoon cayenne pepper</cell>
    </row>
    <row>
      <cell>2 to 3 tablespoons mango chutney or peach jam (optional) </cell>
    </row>
  </tabular>

  <p>Instructions
    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Cook rice with the appropriate amount of water, and turmeric if desired.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add onion and garlic to canola oil and cook it to your satisfaction.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          In a separate pan, cook the chicken. Cut into small pieces.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add curry paste, broth, and cayenne pepper to the onion and garlic.  Cook at medium heat and stir until combined.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add coconut milk to onion and garlic mixture. Heat at medium-high, uncovered, until it starts to bubble.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add chicken to the curry sauce.  Simmer curry sauce at medium heat, uncovered, until it slightly thickens.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Add chutney, if desired, just before serving.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </p>

  <p>
    Notes:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <p>
          
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </p>
</section>